    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## Jordan's Garden Webpage\r\n\r\nJordan wants to make a webpage about a local community garden but doesn't know how to write HTML or CSS. Instead, they've provided you with a description and a potential screenshot:\r\n\r\n> \"I want to make a webpage about the community garden because it's one of my favorite places in the neighborhood and I want more people to know about it. I want a photo of the garden and some writing about it on the page. The writing should be easy to read — not too small. And the photo should look like it has a frame around it.\"\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://images.code.org/744e0df14ca6ade62a64e99905783d6b-image-1774411192443.png\" style=\"width: 40%\" />\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n**Do This:**\r\n1) Use AI tutor to help build this page. Ask it to make changes to this page step-by-step.\r\n    - Be specific about the elements, sizes, borders, and which elements they apply to\r\n2) Keep prompting until the webpage it's \"close enough\" to their vision!\r\n    - It doesn't have to perfectly match the image, but try to get it close to the style and layout!\r\n\r\nOnce you've compared your result to Jordan's vision: press the Continue button!\r\n\r\n**Hint:** This puzzle involves `<p>` and `<img>` tags in HTML, and the `font-size` and `border` properties in CSS.",
